  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Because the addition of maternal effects doubles the number of factors in the linear model for the phenotype, it greatly increases the number of causal components that potentially contribute to the resemblance between relatives. Consider the phenotypic covariance between two individuals — x with mother w, and y with mother z. Assuming no genotype × environment interaction, there are still eight causal components of covariance,",
      "source_page": 701,
      "printed_page": 681,
      "source_block_ids": [
