    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Indeed, if $ \\sigma_{A_{o},A_{m}} $ were sufficiently negative, the regression of offspring on father could be negative. Similar arguments apply to the mother-offspring regression. Such negative regressions have been observed on occasion. For example, Gibbs (1988) observed significant negative mother-offspring regressions for clutch size in Darwin's medium ground finches.",
